2026-11-14T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2494) 'the Mojo guest sample: build, runtime stand-ins, public function and limits.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2494  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2494) 'Can Mojo be a guest language here, with its standard library and async tasks, when Modular ships no RISC-V build of the runtime Mojo's startup calls?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2494  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2494) 'Mojo emits a RISC-V object and links no cross-compiled executable. Its startup calls 28 runtime entry points. Modular publishes those sources, but some headers they include are missing from the tree. The sandbox host also refuses an ELF that does not name its Variant size.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2494  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2494) 'Run the sample in the engine's Sandbox build. It prints through the standard library, adds up three async tasks and answers a vmcall for add_numbers(3, 4) with 7. Then run the limits tests.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2494  1 LINE
 Text:Written

